/* Airline Agent Policy — tau2-airline
 *
 * English source: experiments/translation/spec.md
 * Mode L (trace-grounded). Every structural claim in the K-block below
 * was read off the 88 captured, oracle-labeled decision points in
 * outputs/variant-set/run5/scenarios.json and the trace-derived system
 * profile in outputs/variant-set/run5/system.md.
 *
 * Content checks are deterministic C++ functors in
 * airline_functors.cpp. The policy uses no @llm_check_fn, no
 * ActionMetadata and no ask-kind denials: this deployment (the tau2
 * harness driving sasy.reference_monitor.check_tool_call) supplies an
 * oracle for none of them and surfaces no approval prompt, so a rule
 * resting on one would read as coverage while enforcing nothing.
 *
 * Round-trip audit: PASS (2026-08-20)
 */
#include "../../../../policies/common_policy.dl"

/* ── K-Constraints (verified against the run5 traces) ───────────────

   K1: Two agent names speak in every one of the 88 slices —
       "LLMAgent" (the airline assistant under policy) and
       "UserSimulator" (the simulated customer) — and BOTH emit
       agent_role user, assistant and system. The capture mirrors
       every turn under both names: across the 88 slices there are
       exactly 326 LLMAgent/user, 326 UserSimulator/assistant and 326
       UserSimulator/user messages, and the UserSimulator/user
       messages carry the AGENT's words (node 36b2a5fd… is "Hi! How
       can I help you today?"). Therefore every rule that reads "what
       the customer said" filters BOTH msg.agent = "LLMAgent" AND
       msg.agent_role = $UserRole(). Filtering on the role alone would
       let the agent confirm its own database writes.

   K2: A tool result is a node with agent = "LLMAgent", agent_role =
       $AgentType() and a ToolResult(id, fn_name, args) tuple; its
       msg.contents is the raw result payload. All eleven observed
       tools produce result nodes except transfer_to_human_agents
       (4 calls, 0 result nodes — system.md), so no rule joins on a
       transfer_to_human_agents result.

   K3: Every direct Edge into the Current node carries EdgeData with a
       dense message_index covering the whole linear history (the
       cancel_reservation-86eb603d slice has 30 such edges, indices
       0..29, exactly one with proximal = 1). "The latest customer
       turn" is therefore the LLMAgent/$UserRole() source holding the
       maximal message_index on an edge into Current.

   K4: get_user_details results carry membership as a bare string
       ("regular" | "silver" | "gold") and payment_methods as an
       OBJECT keyed by payment id — not a list. Membership is read
       with @json_get_str and profile membership with
       @json_object_has_key(contents, "payment_methods", pid).

   K5: Reservation-shaped results (get_reservation_details,
       book_reservation, cancel_reservation, update_reservation_*)
       carry reservation_id, cabin, created_at ("2024-05-10T16:48:21"),
       insurance ("yes"/"no"), total_baggages and nonfree_baggages as
       ints, flights as an array of {flight_number, date, price} and
       passengers as an array of {first_name, last_name, dob}. A slice
       routinely holds several different reservations (FDZ0T5 and
       HSR97W in one conversation), so every reservation lookup is
       keyed on the reservation_id INSIDE the payload.

   K6: update_reservation_flights, calculate, search_direct_flight and
       search_onestop_flight results are not JSON objects (error
       strings, bare numbers, arrays — system.md warnings). Field
       accessors return "" on them; no rule depends on their fields.

   K7: Failed calls also produce result nodes ("Error: User
       user_current not found"). Reservation state for the reservation
       being acted on may therefore be absent, so every rule that
       consults reservation state is guarded on that state existing.
       A rule that denied on absence would deny every first touch.

   K8: Slices run 7–84 nodes with at most 2 agent names. The read and
       arithmetic tools (get_reservation_details, search_direct_flight,
       search_onestop_flight, calculate — 50 of the 88 decision
       points) need no graph state at all, so
       CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant is gated to the tools that do.

   K9: Captured decision points carry principal "captured-principal"
       and NO roles (provenance.roles_unknown: true on all 88). No
       airline rule may gate on HasRole — every live call would fail.
   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ── Structured Spec ────────────────────────────────────────────────

   C1  Allow the airline agent's own tool set; deny anything else.
   C2  Deny get_user_details when the user id was never supplied by
       the customer nor returned by an earlier tool call.
   C3  Deny a booking-database write (book, cancel, change flights,
       change baggage, change passengers) unless the latest customer
       turn is an explicit go-ahead.
   C4  A go-ahead conditioned on a figure the agent has not yet
       supplied ("tell me the charge before you finalize") is not an
       explicit go-ahead.
   C5  Deny book_reservation with more than five passengers.
   C6  Deny book_reservation whose passenger dates of birth never
       appeared in the conversation.
   C7  Deny book_reservation using more than one travel certificate,
       more than one credit card, or more than three gift cards — and
       therefore more than five payment methods in total, since those
       are the only three kinds of payment method there are.
   C8  Deny a write whose payment method is not in the customer's
       profile.
   C9  Deny update_reservation_flights that changes the itinerary of a
       basic-economy reservation.
   C10 Deny a reservation update paid with a travel certificate.
   C11 Deny update_reservation_passengers that changes the number of
       passengers.
   C12 Deny update_reservation_baggages that lowers the number of
       checked bags.
   C13 Deny cancel_reservation until the customer has given a reason
       for cancelling.
   C14 Deny cancel_reservation unless the reservation qualifies:
       booked within the last 24 hours, business cabin, or covered by
       travel insurance.
   C15 Deny cancel_reservation, and deny a cabin change, once any
       flight in the reservation has departed.
   C16 Deny send_certificate to a regular member, or before the
       membership level has been verified.
   C17 Deny send_certificate the customer did not ask for.

   Graph assumptions per clause, with trace evidence:
     C2, C6      read every customer turn and every tool result in the
                 backward slice (K1, K2).
     C3, C4      read exactly the latest customer turn, located by
                 message_index on the edges into Current (K3).
     C8, C16     read get_user_details payloads (K4).
     C9, C11,
     C12, C14,
     C15         read reservation payloads keyed by the payload's own
                 reservation_id (K5), guarded on presence (K7).
     C13, C17    read every customer turn in the slice (K1).

   Deliberately not encoded, and why:
     · "cannot change origin, destination or trip type" —
       update_reservation_flights arguments carry only flight_number
       and date (system.md argument fields), so the route a proposed
       itinerary implies is not visible at the decision point.
     · "cannot add insurance after booking" — no update tool takes an
       insurance argument, so the action is unreachable.
     · "one tool call at a time", "no unsupported information or
        subjective recommendations", "transfer only when out of
       scope" — these constrain the agent's prose, which the tool-call
       decision point does not carry.
     · C14's airline-cancellation branch — whether the airline
       cancelled a flight lives in get_flight_status output, which no
       captured slice contains; the branch is folded into the
       insurance and 24-hour branches rather than guessed at.

   Known limits of what is encoded:
     · C8 only fires once the customer's profile is in the slice. An
       agent that pays without ever calling get_user_details is not
       stopped by it — the alternative, denying every payment until a
       profile has been read, would deny first-touch bookings the
       captured traffic makes routinely.
     · Reservation state is whatever any payload in the slice shows,
       not the newest payload. Bag counts and passenger counts only
       move in the direction the policy already allows, and
       cancellation eligibility takes any qualifying payload, so the
       looseness is one-directional. C9 is the exception and reads
       the newest cabin explicitly.
     · C6 checks the first five passengers and C8 the first five
       payment methods. C5 and C7 deny anything longer, so no
       element escapes both.
   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* ── Custom content functors (airline_functors.cpp) ─────────────── */

.functor user_confirms(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor confirmation_deferred(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor payment_last_four(profile: symbol, pid: symbol): symbol stateful
.functor cancel_reason(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor compensation_requested(text: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor contains_ci(hay: symbol, needle: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor flights_differ(args: symbol, payload: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor any_flight_departed(payload: symbol, today: symbol): unsigned stateful
.functor count_payment_prefix(args: symbol, prefix: symbol): unsigned stateful

/* ── Tool taxonomy (C1) ─────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* C1: the tools this agent is allowed to call at all. */
.decl AirlineTool(name: symbol)
AirlineTool("get_user_details").
AirlineTool("get_reservation_details").
AirlineTool("get_flight_status").
AirlineTool("search_direct_flight").
AirlineTool("search_onestop_flight").
AirlineTool("calculate").
AirlineTool("think").
AirlineTool("book_reservation").
AirlineTool("cancel_reservation").
AirlineTool("update_reservation_flights").
AirlineTool("update_reservation_passengers").
AirlineTool("update_reservation_baggages").
AirlineTool("send_certificate").
AirlineTool("transfer_to_human_agents").

/* C3: the writes that change the booking database. */
.decl DbWriteTool(name: symbol)
DbWriteTool("book_reservation").
DbWriteTool("cancel_reservation").
DbWriteTool("update_reservation_flights").
DbWriteTool("update_reservation_passengers").
DbWriteTool("update_reservation_baggages").

/* C8, C10: the updates that take a single payment_id argument. */
.decl UpdatePayTool(name: symbol)
UpdatePayTool("update_reservation_flights").
UpdatePayTool("update_reservation_baggages").

/* K5: the tools whose results carry a full reservation payload.
   update_reservation_flights is absent by K6 — its result is an
   error string or a bare confirmation, never a JSON object. */
.decl ResPayloadTool(name: symbol)
ResPayloadTool("get_reservation_details").
ResPayloadTool("book_reservation").
ResPayloadTool("cancel_reservation").
ResPayloadTool("update_reservation_passengers").
ResPayloadTool("update_reservation_baggages").

/* K8: only these actions consult prior graph state. Gating the
   traversal here keeps the 50 read/arithmetic decision points from
   walking their slice at all. */
.decl NeedsGraphState(name: symbol)
NeedsGraphState(n) :- DbWriteTool(n).
NeedsGraphState("get_user_details").
NeedsGraphState("send_certificate").

CurrentDependsPolicyRelevant() :-
    Actions(_, a),
    IsTool(a, name),
    NeedsGraphState(name).

/* Small bounded index sets for walking JSON arrays. Five is the
   passenger ceiling the policy itself sets (C5); a booking with more
   passengers than that is denied by C5 regardless. */
.decl PassengerIdx(i: unsigned)
PassengerIdx(0). PassengerIdx(1). PassengerIdx(2).
PassengerIdx(3). PassengerIdx(4).

.decl PaymentIdx(i: unsigned)
PaymentIdx(0). PaymentIdx(1). PaymentIdx(2).
PaymentIdx(3). PaymentIdx(4).

/* ── Conversation view ──────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* K1: a turn the CUSTOMER wrote. The msg.agent filter is what keeps
   the mirrored UserSimulator/$UserRole() turns — which carry the
   agent's own words — out of every content rule below. */
.decl CustomerTurn(id: symbol)
CustomerTurn(id) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    msg.agent = "LLMAgent",
    msg.agent_role = $UserRole().

/* K3: customer turns positioned in the linear history of the action
   under evaluation. */
.decl CustomerTurnAt(mi: number, id: symbol)
CustomerTurnAt(mi, src) :-
    Current(dst),
    EdgeData(src, dst, ed),
    mi = ed.message_index,
    mi >= 0,
    SentMessage(src, msg),
    msg.agent = "LLMAgent",
    msg.agent_role = $UserRole().

.decl SupersededCustomerTurn(mi: number)
SupersededCustomerTurn(m1) :-
    CustomerTurnAt(m1, _),
    CustomerTurnAt(m2, _),
    m2 > m1.

.decl LatestCustomerTurn(id: symbol)
LatestCustomerTurn(id) :-
    CustomerTurnAt(mi, id),
    !SupersededCustomerTurn(mi).

.decl LatestCustomerText(text: symbol)
LatestCustomerText(text) :-
    LatestCustomerTurn(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    text = msg.contents.

/* C3: a general go-ahead in the latest customer turn confirms
   whatever the agent listed. C4 is folded into @user_confirms: a turn
   that defers on a figure the agent still owes is not a go-ahead. */
.decl GeneralGoAhead()
GeneralGoAhead() :-
    LatestCustomerText(text),
    @user_confirms(text) = 1.

/* C4: the same deferral, isolated so it also vetoes the
   payment-instrument route below. */
.decl GoAheadDeferred()
GoAheadDeferred() :-
    LatestCustomerText(text),
    @confirmation_deferred(text) = 1.

/* K1, K2: text the agent may treat as established fact — what the
   customer wrote, and what the tools returned. The agent's own prose
   is deliberately excluded: a detail the agent invented and then
   restated does not become grounded by being restated. */
.decl GroundingText(text: symbol)
GroundingText(text) :-
    CustomerTurn(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    text = msg.contents.
GroundingText(text) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, _, _),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    text = msg.contents.

/* ── Reservation and profile state (K5, K7) ─────────────────────── */

.decl ResPayload(rid: symbol, payload: symbol)
ResPayload(rid, payload) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, tool, _),
    ResPayloadTool(tool),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    payload = msg.contents,
    rid = @json_get_str(payload, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "".

/* K7: guard predicate — is anything known about this reservation? */
.decl ResKnown(rid: symbol)
ResKnown(rid) :- ResPayload(rid, _).

.decl ResCabin(rid: symbol, cabin: symbol)
ResCabin(rid, cabin) :-
    ResPayload(rid, payload),
    cabin = @json_get_str(payload, "cabin"),
    cabin != "".

.decl ResCreatedAt(rid: symbol, ts: symbol)
ResCreatedAt(rid, ts) :-
    ResPayload(rid, payload),
    ts = @json_get_str(payload, "created_at"),
    ts != "".

.decl ResInsurance(rid: symbol, ins: symbol)
ResInsurance(rid, ins) :-
    ResPayload(rid, payload),
    ins = @json_get_str(payload, "insurance"),
    ins != "".

.decl ResTotalBaggages(rid: symbol, bags: number)
ResTotalBaggages(rid, bags) :-
    ResPayload(rid, payload),
    @json_has_field(payload, "total_baggages") = 1,
    bags = @json_get_int(payload, "total_baggages").

.decl ResPassengerCount(rid: symbol, n: unsigned)
ResPassengerCount(rid, n) :-
    ResPayload(rid, payload),
    n = @json_array_len(payload, "passengers"),
    n > 0.

/* K4: payment instruments on the customer's profile. Reservation
   payment history counts too — an instrument the reservation was
   already charged to is on file by construction. */
.decl ProfilePayload(payload: symbol)
ProfilePayload(payload) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, "get_user_details", _),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    payload = msg.contents,
    @json_has_field(payload, "payment_methods") = 1.

.decl ProfileKnown()
ProfileKnown() :- ProfilePayload(_).

.decl CandidatePayment(idx: unsigned, pid: symbol)
CandidatePayment(idx, pid) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, args),
    UpdatePayTool(fn),
    pid = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    pid != "".
CandidatePayment(idx, pid) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    PaymentIdx(i),
    n = @json_array_len(args, "payment_methods"),
    i < n,
    pid = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "payment_methods", i, "payment_id"),
    pid != "".

.decl ProfilePayment(pid: symbol)
ProfilePayment(pid) :-
    CandidatePayment(_, pid),
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, "get_user_details", _),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    @json_object_has_key(msg.contents, "payment_methods", pid) = 1.
ProfilePayment(pid) :-
    CandidatePayment(_, pid),
    ResPayload(_, payload),
    @str_contains(payload, pid) = 1.

/* C3: the second route to confirmation. When the customer names the
   instrument to charge — by its id, or by the last four digits the
   profile records for it ("you can use my credit card ending in
   3848") — that authorizes the action that charges THAT instrument,
   and only that one. Charging a different instrument still needs its
   own go-ahead. */
.decl PaymentNamedByCustomer(idx: unsigned, pid: symbol)
PaymentNamedByCustomer(idx, pid) :-
    CandidatePayment(idx, pid),
    LatestCustomerText(text),
    @contains_ci(text, pid) = 1.
PaymentNamedByCustomer(idx, pid) :-
    CandidatePayment(idx, pid),
    LatestCustomerText(text),
    ProfilePayload(payload),
    digits = @payment_last_four(payload, pid),
    digits != "",
    @str_contains(text, digits) = 1.

.decl PaymentUnnamed(idx: unsigned)
PaymentUnnamed(idx) :-
    CandidatePayment(idx, pid),
    !PaymentNamedByCustomer(idx, pid).

/* C3, C4: the action carries the customer's go-ahead, by either
   route. C4's deferral vetoes both. */
.decl ConfirmedForAction(idx: unsigned)
ConfirmedForAction(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, _),
    GeneralGoAhead().
ConfirmedForAction(idx) :-
    CandidatePayment(idx, _),
    !PaymentUnnamed(idx),
    !GoAheadDeferred().

/* K4: membership level, keyed on the profile's own user_id so two
   customers in one slice never mix. */
.decl UserMembership(uid: symbol, level: symbol)
UserMembership(uid, level) :-
    CurrentDepends(id),
    ToolResult(id, "get_user_details", _),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    uid = @json_get_str(msg.contents, "user_id"),
    uid != "",
    level = @json_get_str(msg.contents, "membership"),
    level != "".

.decl MembershipKnown(uid: symbol)
MembershipKnown(uid) :- UserMembership(uid, _).

/* ── C1: allowlist ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */

/* C1: the agent's own tools are authorized; every denial below carves
   out of this one rule. Anything not on the list has no allow rule
   and is refused by default. */
IsAuthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, name),
    AirlineTool(name).

/* C1: replying to the customer is not a database action and carries
   no argument the policy can check; message sends pass through. */
IsAuthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $SendAttempt(_).

DenyUnauthorized(idx) :- Actions(idx, _).

/* ── C2: the user id must come from the customer ────────────────── */

.decl RequestedUserId(idx: unsigned, uid: symbol)
RequestedUserId(idx, uid) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "get_user_details"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    uid != "".

.decl UserIdGrounded(uid: symbol)
UserIdGrounded(uid) :-
    RequestedUserId(_, uid),
    GroundingText(text),
    @contains_ci(text, uid) = 1.

// @deny_message: The user id was never provided by the customer or returned by an earlier tool call, so it cannot be looked up.
// @suggestion: Ask the customer for their user id, or locate their profile from a reservation id they give you, before calling get_user_details.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    RequestedUserId(idx, uid),
    !UserIdGrounded(uid).

/* ── C3, C4: explicit confirmation before any database write ────── */

// @deny_message: This action changes the booking database and the customer has not given an explicit go-ahead for it.
// @suggestion: List the exact action details — flights, cabin, passengers, bags, payment method and amount — answer any figure the customer asked for first, then ask them to confirm with 'yes' and call the tool only after they do.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, name),
    DbWriteTool(name),
    !ConfirmedForAction(idx).

/* ── C5, C6, C7, C8: booking a reservation ──────────────────────── */

// @deny_message: A reservation can carry at most five passengers.
// @suggestion: Split the party across several reservations of at most five passengers each.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @json_array_len(args, "passengers"),
    n > 5.

.decl BookedPassengerDob(idx: unsigned, dob: symbol)
BookedPassengerDob(idx, dob) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    PassengerIdx(i),
    n = @json_array_len(args, "passengers"),
    i < n,
    dob = @json_array_get_field_str(args, "passengers", i, "dob"),
    dob != "".

.decl DobGrounded(dob: symbol)
DobGrounded(dob) :-
    BookedPassengerDob(_, dob),
    GroundingText(text),
    @str_contains(text, dob) = 1.

// @deny_message: A passenger's date of birth on this booking never appeared in the conversation, so it was not collected from the customer.
// @suggestion: Ask the customer for the first name, last name and date of birth of every passenger, and book only the details they give you.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    BookedPassengerDob(idx, dob),
    !DobGrounded(dob).

// @deny_message: A reservation may use at most one travel certificate.
// @suggestion: Use a single certificate on this reservation and cover the rest with gift cards or a credit card, or split the party into separate reservations.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "certificate"),
    n > 1.

// @deny_message: A reservation may use at most one credit card.
// @suggestion: Choose one credit card for this reservation.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "credit_card"),
    n > 1.

// @deny_message: A reservation may use at most three gift cards.
// @suggestion: Use at most three gift cards and cover any remainder with a credit card or a travel certificate.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @count_payment_prefix(args, "gift_card"),
    n > 3.

// @deny_message: A reservation may use at most five payment methods — one travel certificate, one credit card and three gift cards.
// @suggestion: Reduce the booking to at most one certificate, one credit card and three gift cards, or split the party into separate reservations.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "book_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    n = @json_array_len(args, "payment_methods"),
    n > 5.

// @deny_message: That payment method is not on the customer's profile, and only stored payment methods may be used.
// @suggestion: Read the customer's profile with get_user_details and pay with one of the payment methods listed there.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    CandidatePayment(idx, pid),
    ProfileKnown(),
    !ProfilePayment(pid).

/* ── C9, C10: changing flights and cabin ────────────────────────── */

/* K7: a reservation the conversation has also shown in some other
   cabin is not a basic-economy reservation any more — an earlier
   payload from before an upgrade must not bar a later flight change.
   update_reservation_flights results are not JSON (K6), so the newer
   cabin only appears once the agent re-reads the reservation. */
.decl ResCabinOtherThanBasic(rid: symbol)
ResCabinOtherThanBasic(rid) :-
    ResCabin(rid, cabin),
    cabin != "basic_economy".


// @deny_message: Basic economy flights cannot be changed.
// @suggestion: Explain that a basic economy itinerary cannot be modified. The cabin alone can still be changed, and the reservation can be cancelled if it qualifies.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "",
    ResCabin(rid, "basic_economy"),
    !ResCabinOtherThanBasic(rid),
    ResPayload(rid, payload),
    @flights_differ(args, payload) = 1.

// @deny_message: A reservation update must be paid with a single gift card or credit card; a travel certificate cannot be used.
// @suggestion: Ask the customer for a gift card or credit card on their profile and pay the difference with that.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    a = $CallTool(fn, args),
    UpdatePayTool(fn),
    pid = @json_get_str(args, "payment_id"),
    @str_starts_with(pid, "certificate") = 1.

/* ── C11: the number of passengers is fixed ─────────────────────── */

// @deny_message: The number of passengers on a reservation cannot be changed — not by this agent and not by a human agent.
// @suggestion: Passenger details can be corrected as long as the count stays the same. To travel with a different number of people the reservation must be cancelled, if it qualifies, and rebooked.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_passengers"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "",
    ResPassengerCount(rid, was),
    now = @json_array_len(args, "passengers"),
    now != was.

/* ── C12: checked bags can be added, not removed ────────────────── */

// @deny_message: Checked bags can be added to a reservation but not removed.
// @suggestion: Explain that bags already on the reservation cannot be taken off and are not refundable; only additional bags can be booked.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_baggages"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "",
    ResTotalBaggages(rid, was),
    now = @json_get_int(args, "total_baggages"),
    now < was.

/* ── C13, C14, C15: cancelling ──────────────────────────────────── */

.decl CancelTarget(idx: unsigned, rid: symbol)
CancelTarget(idx, rid) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "cancel_reservation"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "".

.decl CancellationReasonGiven()
CancellationReasonGiven() :-
    CustomerTurn(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    @cancel_reason(msg.contents) = 1.

// @deny_message: The customer has not given a reason for cancelling, and the reason decides whether the cancellation is allowed.
// @suggestion: Ask whether this is a change of plan, a flight the airline cancelled, or another reason, and record the answer before cancelling.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    CancelTarget(idx, _),
    !CancellationReasonGiven().

/* C14: the reservation qualifies for cancellation. The spec's
   airline-cancellation branch is not represented — see the spec block
   above. hours_between returns an absolute difference, so the >= 0
   guard only rejects its -1 parse failure. */
.decl CancelEligible(rid: symbol)
CancelEligible(rid) :-
    ResCreatedAt(rid, ts),
    h = @hours_between(ts, "2024-05-15T15:00:00"),
    h >= 0,
    h < 24.
CancelEligible(rid) :- ResCabin(rid, "business").
CancelEligible(rid) :- ResInsurance(rid, "yes").

// @deny_message: This reservation does not qualify for cancellation — it was not booked in the last 24 hours, it is not a business cabin booking, and it has no travel insurance.
// @suggestion: Explain which conditions allow a cancellation and that none of them apply here. If the airline itself cancelled a flight on this reservation, confirm that with get_flight_status first.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    CancelTarget(idx, rid),
    ResKnown(rid),
    !CancelEligible(rid).

.decl ResHasDepartedFlight(rid: symbol)
ResHasDepartedFlight(rid) :-
    ResPayload(rid, payload),
    @any_flight_departed(payload, "2024-05-15") = 1.

// @deny_message: Part of this trip has already been flown, so the agent cannot cancel it.
// @suggestion: Call transfer_to_human_agents with a summary, then tell the customer 'YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON.'
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    CancelTarget(idx, rid),
    ResHasDepartedFlight(rid).

// @deny_message: The cabin cannot be changed once a flight on the reservation has been flown.
// @suggestion: Explain that the cabin is fixed for a trip already under way. Call transfer_to_human_agents if the customer needs more than this agent can do.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "update_reservation_flights"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    rid = @json_get_str(args, "reservation_id"),
    rid != "",
    cabin = @json_get_str(args, "cabin"),
    cabin != "",
    ResCabin(rid, was),
    cabin != was,
    ResHasDepartedFlight(rid).

/* ── C16, C17: compensation ─────────────────────────────────────── */

.decl CertTarget(idx: unsigned, uid: symbol)
CertTarget(idx, uid) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    a = $CallTool(_, args),
    uid = @json_get_str(args, "user_id"),
    uid != "".

// @deny_message: Membership level has not been verified, and only silver and gold members are eligible for compensation.
// @suggestion: Call get_user_details for this customer and check the membership field before offering anything.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    CertTarget(idx, uid),
    !MembershipKnown(uid).

// @deny_message: Regular members are not eligible for compensation, whatever the cabin, insurance or reason.
// @suggestion: Explain that compensation is available to silver and gold members only. A claim to be a higher tier does not change the profile's membership level.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    CertTarget(idx, uid),
    UserMembership(uid, "regular").

.decl CompensationRequested()
CompensationRequested() :-
    CustomerTurn(id),
    SentMessage(id, msg),
    @compensation_requested(msg.contents) = 1.

// @deny_message: Compensation must not be offered unless the customer asks for it.
// @suggestion: Resolve what the customer actually asked about. Send a certificate only if they ask for compensation and you have confirmed the cancelled or delayed flight.
Unauthorized(idx) :-
    Actions(idx, a),
    IsTool(a, "send_certificate"),
    !CompensationRequested().
